/github.com/DertolleDude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DertolleDude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-25T18:04:54Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T18:04:54Z","body":"I experienced the same issue in my 2d project. I tried some older Nvidia driver versions and with version 577.0 I get a lot less stutter. I am not sure if it is fixed completely since I occasionally still get a small stutter, but these could be unrelated to this issue.\nAnother thing I noticed is that the line of the FPS monitor in Godot is pretty much entirely flat when capping the framerate to a value lower than the refresh rate but very jagged when the fps is capped at the refresh rate of my display. This behavior is the same with driver 577.0.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3221229386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3304621319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109686#issuecomment-3304621319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109686","id":3304621319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E-IUH","user":{"login":"automatika-mega","id":232940971,"node_id":"U_kgDODeJlqw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232940971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega","html_url":"https://github.com/automatika-mega","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T21:28:54Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T21:30:00Z","body":"Seems like its an nvidia driver issue, rolling back to 576.52 fixed the issue for me. https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/forums/game-ready-drivers/13/574380/geforce-grd-58129-feedback-thread-released-91025/3564432/ and https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/forums/game-ready-drivers/13/573152/regression-vsync-is-very-choppy-on-godot-engine-ga","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3304621319/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358631901","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109686#issuecomment-3358631901","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109686","id":3358631901,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IMKfd","user":{"login":"nearlytobias","id":65813194,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODEzMTk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65813194?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias","html_url":"https://github.com/nearlytobias","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nearlytobias/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-02T00:43:54Z","updated_at":"2025-10-02T00:43:54Z","body":"This has supposedly been tackled in the latest Nvidia driver (581.42). Info here: https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/drivers/details/257133/\n\nI have seen a forum response that suggests it's still an issue with certain settings: https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/forums/game-ready-drivers/13/575454/geforce-grd-58142-feedback-thread-released-93025/3566982/\n\nSo something to test on your personal set up","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358631901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3403455946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109686#issuecomment-3403455946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109686","id":3403455946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7K3J3K","user":{"login":"automatika-mega","id":232940971,"node_id":"U_kgDODeJlqw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232940971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega","html_url":"https://github.com/automatika-mega","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automatika-mega/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T20:13:54Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T20:17:33Z","body":"With 581.42, they managed to fix the stutter in VSYNC_ENABLED, but the stutter continues in VSYNC_ADAPTIVE and VSYNC_MAILBOX. Also the new driver has now introduced stuttering in VSYNC_DISABLED.\n\nif you also have this issue use this link https://nvidia.custhelp.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/3507 to share feedback for low FPS/stutter/performance issues using GPUView","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3403455946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6269469295","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109686#issuecomment-6269469295","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109686","id":6269469295,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdbCCbw","user":{"login":"Ark2000","id":21126555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTI2NTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21126555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000","html_url":"https://github.com/Ark2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ark2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T14:20:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T14:20:36Z","body":"I can reproduce this on Godot 4.7.2 with a project that contains nothing but one `ColorRect`, and **Mailbox** gets rid of it here.\n\n**System:** Windows 11 (build 26100), laptop with NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Laptop GPU, Vulkan 1.4.329, Godot v4.7.2.stable.mono, Forward+, display at about 180 Hz, windowed.\n\n**Minimal project** (`project.godot` with only `config/name` and `renderer/rendering_method=\"forward_plus\"`, main scene is a `ColorRect` with this script):\n\n```gdscript\nextends ColorRect\nvar t := 0.0\nvar n := 0\nvar worst := 0.0\nfunc _process(d):\n\tt += d\n\tif t > 3.0 and d > 0.02:\n\t\tn += 1\n\t\tworst = max(worst, d)\n\t\tprint(\"SPIKE %.1fms at %.1fs\" % [d * 1000, t])\n\tif t > 15.0:\n\t\tprint(\"RESULT spikes>20ms: %d worst %.1fms\" % [n, worst * 1000])\n\t\tget_tree().quit()\n```\n\n**Result:** number of frames with a delta above 20 ms between 3 s and 15 s, one number per 15 s run, FPS cap not set:\n\n| mode | runs |\n|---|---|\n| `VSYNC_ENABLED` (default) | 5, 7, 17 (spikes 22 to 50 ms) |\n| `VSYNC_DISABLED` | 1, 1 |\n| `VSYNC_ADAPTIVE` | 31, 25 |\n| `VSYNC_MAILBOX` | 0, 0 |\n| `--rendering-method gl_compatibility`, vsync on | 0 (one run) |\n\nI did not test D3D12. The spikes show up with no input and without alt-tabbing, a few times per second to once every few seconds, so they look like missed vblanks and not a load problem (the real project this started from measured under 1 ms of CPU and 5 ms of GPU per frame at 180 fps).\n\n**Workaround that works here:** set `DisplayServer.window_set_vsync_mode(DisplayServer.VSYNC_MAILBOX)` and set `Engine.max_fps` to the screen refresh rate yourself (Mailbox does not wait for the display, so without a cap it renders as fast as it can). With that, the frame time graph of a full 3D game is flat again.\n\nThis looks like the same thing as the reports in #84137 and #71391, and the pattern described here (Vulkan + Forward+ + VSync on, gone with VSync off or another API).\n\nWritten with the help of Claude Code, from measurements made on the machine described above.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6269469295/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]